message:
Running command: cd /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul && grep -rn "strtoul\|strtoull" --include="*.c" --include="*.h" Zend/zend_ini.c ext/standard/basic_functions.c ext/standard/scanf.c ext/standard/crypt_sha512.c ext/standard/crypt_sha256.c 2>/dev/null | head; echo "---these use ZEND_STRTOUL which is strtoull on 64-bit. The __isoc23_strtoull comes from gcc12 with _GNU_SOURCE? Let me check if a simple gcc compile of strtoull produces __isoc23---"; cat > /tmp/t.c <<'EOF'
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <errno.h>
unsigned long f(const char*s){return strtoul(s,NULL,10);}
unsigned long long g(const char*s){return strtoull(s,NULL,10);}
double h(double a,double b){return fmod(a,b);}
EOF
gcc -O2 -std=gnu17 -D_GNU_SOURCE -c /tmp/t.c -o /tmp/t.o 2>&1 | head; nm /tmp/t.o | grep -i "strtoul\|fmod"

